  "summary": "A painting technique emphasizing the subtle gradations of black ink to create depth and atmosphere.",
  "description": "Sumi-e uses diluted ink applied with varying pressure to create subtle tonal transitions from deep black to near-white, capturing the essence of subjects rather than detailed representation. This technique developed from Chinese landscape painting traditions and was refined in Japan, embodying Zen Buddhist principles of simplicity and impermanence.",
